Upstream: https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty/pull/14849
  "core: let cmd-click open links while the mouse is captured" (open,
  unmerged at the pinned commit; upstream commit efff3c72)

While a program captures the mouse (tmux, Claude Code fullscreen, and
similar TUIs), the pinned core only refreshes link state for the shift
bypass. A plain Command-click therefore never marks a link as hovered
and is reported to the program, which cannot distinguish it from a
plain click because mouse reports cannot encode Super.

Rebased on the current upstream PR, which adds `link_press`: Super
activates link detection under capture, and a Super-press on a link
stays out of the mouse report entirely — press, motion, and release —
with the selection gesture reset, so the existing release path opens
the link. Without it, a cmd-click with a little trackpad drift inside
tmux sends a drag the program never saw start. Keeps the local
`mouseLinksActiveFor` split so the modifier/capture truth table stays
unit-tested.

Carried here because it is unmerged upstream. Drop this file when the
pin reaches a commit that already has it.

